WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:06.465
The new MES, the system that runs the orders on the floor, has to go to more lines.

2
00:00:07.258 --> 00:00:10.021
One IT team is too small for the whole system.

3
00:00:11.057 --> 00:00:13.286
You lead the project for the plant manager.

4
00:00:13.996 --> 00:00:15.494
More IT teams join.

5
00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:19.710
We follow this project through the four topics of the module.

6
00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:23.177
The first topic is SAFe basics.

7
00:00:23.906 --> 00:00:26.275
How do you make many teams work as one whole?

8
00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:30.558
Each team can work fine and the whole still gets stuck.

9
00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:33.118
Team A waits for team B.

10
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.527
That is called a dependency.

11
00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:40.065
SAFe puts the teams on a train, the Agile Release Train.

12
00:00:40.735 --> 00:00:44.891
The teams stay together for a long time and build one product together.

13
00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:49.099
The train works to one fixed rhythm, the cadence.

14
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:53.554
All teams plan, build and deliver at the same moments.

15
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.383
For SAFe we often use PI Planning, the planning with all teams,

16
00:00:58.569 --> 00:01:00.299
and the ART Planning Board.

17
00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:04.863
The second topic is Portfolio and Lean budgets.

18
00:01:05.587 --> 00:01:08.536
Which work do the teams get, and who pays for it?

19
00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:13.707
All the development investments of the plant together are called the portfolio.

20
00:01:14.454 --> 00:01:16.254
The MES is one of them.

21
00:01:17.286 --> 00:01:22.313
With project funding each project gets its own budget and a temporary team.

22
00:01:23.008 --> 00:01:26.190
SAFe funds the train, and the work comes to the train.

23
00:01:27.185 --> 00:01:30.970
A few strategic themes give the direction for the plant manager.

24
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.811
For the portfolio we often use a Lean business case and a Portfolio Kanban.

25
00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:41.076
The third topic is Alternatives and criticism.

26
00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:45.538
SAFe is not the only way, there are also LeSS and Nexus.

27
00:01:46.692 --> 00:01:48.666
LeSS takes things away instead.

28
00:01:49.382 --> 00:01:52.563
All teams share one Product Owner and one backlog.

29
00:01:53.608 --> 00:01:55.291
It works with feature teams.

30
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.525
Such a team builds a customer function from start to finish.

31
00:02:00.554 --> 00:02:05.651
Alternatives include Sprint Planning One of LeSS and Cross-Team Refinement of Nexus.

32
00:02:06.945 --> 00:02:10.358
The fourth topic is Hybrid, stage-gate plus agile.

33
00:02:11.073 --> 00:02:12.501
What if hardware joins in?

34
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.853
The MES gets a link to scales on the lines.

35
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:21.563
That is hardware, and with hardware the cost of change rises fast.

36
00:02:22.623 --> 00:02:24.840
In stage-gate you work in stages.

37
00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:29.949
Between two stages sits a gate, a decision moment for the plant manager.

38
00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:33.821
Within each stage the teams work in sprints.

39
00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:36.735
The gates stay for the big decisions.

40
00:02:37.722 --> 00:02:41.832
For hybrid work we often use backward planning and a design freeze,

41
00:02:41.972 --> 00:02:42.994
fixing the design.

42
00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.438
It all connects.

43
00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:49.510
SAFe basics gives the train, the portfolio the budget,

44
00:02:49.742 --> 00:02:53.132
the alternatives other ways and hybrid work the hardware.

45
00:02:54.155 --> 00:02:57.859
Scaling means agreements that let many teams deliver as one.

46
00:02:59.177 --> 00:03:00.872
This is the map of Projects.

47
00:03:01.611 --> 00:03:04.769
Scaling is the second station of IT and agile.

48
00:03:05.779 --> 00:03:08.832
Scaling has four topics, each with four levels.

49
00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.378
Start with SAFe basics.

50
00:03:12.095 --> 00:03:17.110
At Basics level it is about why scale, value streams, LeSS and stage-gate.

51
00:03:18.192 --> 00:03:23.208
At Working knowledge you add PI Planning, epics, Nexus and long lead times.

52
00:03:24.229 --> 00:03:27.863
At Advanced you add the roles, scoring with WSJF,

53
00:03:28.049 --> 00:03:30.835
the Spotify model and integration points.

54
00:03:31.866 --> 00:03:34.687
At Expert you add the four configurations,

55
00:03:34.896 --> 00:03:39.273
Lean budgets, the criticism of SAFe and steering a hybrid approach.

56
00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:44.393
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
